{"to":"C","text":"Thanks for reaching out — I'll facilitate this for the three of you and keep a shared list of concerns so nothing gets lost. I'm not deciding anything and can't move money or give legal advice.

Starting point: I'll ask each of you one question.

For you: what matters to you about the trailer, and why? Not what you want to happen — what's the thing underneath it that you'd want me to get right."}

{"text":"That's useful. Let me try to put it in plain words and you tell me if it fits:

Entry 1 — "C wants to be able to count on getting real use of the trailer for their own project, on a timetable they can plan around, rather than their plans depending on when someone else is done."

Does that fit? If a word is off, say which. (And if there's something more underneath — say, being treated as an equal owner, or not being the one who always yields — tell me and I'll add it.)","to":"C"}

{"text":"Thank you — and noted that you're not looking to blame anyone. Let me try to put it in plain words and you tell me if it fits:

